  "subdivision_of_building": "It affect the rear gate external access at ground floor  on 1 Drysdale street.",
  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "This application seeks approval to remove the existing solid shutters and replace them with a porous mesh fence to enclose the rear area of the building and to add additional lighting to the area for security and a CCTV. The proposal aims to facilitate and optimise back-of-house operations, including loading and deliveries to the premises, while also improving safety and site management. The site is located on 1 Drysdale Street is part of Kashette site boundary and represent the rear access to the commercial units on 347-349 Old Street, London, EC1V 9LP . ",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposal, by reason of its detailed design and siting, would have a detrimental impact upon the character and appearance of the streetscene and would fail to&amp;nbsp;preserve or enhance the character and appearance of the adjacent Kingsland Conservation Area. As such, the proposal is contrary to policies D3 (Optimising site capacity through the design-led approach), D4 (Delivering good design), and HC1 (Heritage conservation and growth) of The London Plan (2021), and policies LP1 (Design Quality and Local Character), and LP3 (Designated Heritage Assets) of the Hackney Local Plan (2020) and Hackney&#x27;s Commercial Extensions and Alterations SPD (2025).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
